 **Edge Cases and Pitfalls:**
-*   **Coordinate System:** The view matrix may require specific sign flips on elements $[0][1], [1][0], [1][2], [2][1], [3][1]$ before inversion to adjust for coordinate system differences between the renderer and the camera model [S2, unofficial].
-*   **Precision:** Floating-point precision in WebGL 1.0 may affect large scenes; however, the method is designed to work within standard constraints [S1, unofficial].
 *   **Sorting:** Incorrect sorting order leads to visual artifacts due to non-commutative alpha blending. The sorting must be updated every frame as the camera moves [S2, unofficial].
 
